From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: sky1: defer child probe until wrapper is ready

Sky1 ACPI describes each USB controller as a CIXH2030 wrapper with a
CIXH2031 cdns-usbssp child.  The child platform device is ACPI-enumerated
independently, so its cdnsp_plat_probe() can run before the wrapper probe
has completed the hardware bring-up and runtime-PM activation sequence.

When that happens, cdnsp_plat_probe() reaches:

        pm_runtime_set_active(child);
        pm_runtime_enable(child);

while the CIXH2030 parent is still runtime-suspended/unfinished, producing
one warning pair per controller at boot:

        runtime PM trying to activate child device CIXH2031:0N
        but parent (CIXH2030:0N) is not active
        Enabling runtime PM for inactive device with active children

Patch 0180 moved the wrapper's own PM activation before its child setup, but
ACPI can still probe the already-created CIXH2031 child before the wrapper
has reached that point.  Add an explicit wrapper-ready flag and make Sky1
ACPI children return -EPROBE_DEFER until the parent has completed its setup.

This keeps the CIXH2030 wrapper pinned by its active children; it does not
restore pm_suspend_ignore_children(), which was shown to let the wrapper
runtime-suspend underneath active xHCI children and lose port-change events.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c |  1 +
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
index b58cc37..81de2cb 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-plat.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <linux/property.h>
 
 #include "core.h"
+#include "cdnsp-sky1.h"
 #include "gadget-export.h"
 #include "drd.h"
 
@@ -108,6 +109,30 @@ static void set_phy_power_off(struct cdns *cdns)
 	phy_power_off(cdns->usb2_phy);
 }
 
+static const struct acpi_device_id cdnsp_sky1_parent_match[] = {
+	{ "CIXH2030" },
+	{ }
+};
+
+static int cdnsp_sky1_wait_for_parent(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct device *parent = dev->parent;
+	struct cdnsp_sky1 *data;
+
+	if (!has_acpi_companion(dev) || !parent)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (!acpi_match_device(cdnsp_sky1_parent_match, parent))
+		return 0;
+
+	data = dev_get_drvdata(parent);
+	if (!data || !data->ready)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "waiting for Sky1 USB wrapper\n");
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /**
  * cdnsp_plat_probe - probe for cdnsp core device
  * @pdev: Pointer to cdnsp core platform device
@@ -122,6 +147,10 @@ static int cdnsp_plat_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	void __iomem *regs;
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = cdnsp_sky1_wait_for_parent(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	cdns = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*cdns), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!cdns)
 		return -ENOMEM;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index 46094b0..0400779 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -825,6 +825,7 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	data->ready = true;
 	return 0;
 err_pm:
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
index 82563bd..7cf6ac3 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.h
@@ -116,6 +116,7 @@ struct cdnsp_sky1 {
 	int sof_clk_freq;
 	bool u3_disable;
 	bool ssp_disable;
+	bool ready;
 	int axi_bmax_value;
 	struct gpio_desc *oc_gpio;
 };
-- 
2.51.0
